From 4f9bf718a261fd83ea1511317484e97861b6533d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:37:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban quota hold: report when a fallback route
 opens, not only the walled route's reset

Problem: hub 2026-11-14 09:20Z, 8 unpinned default cards (kanban.default_model gpt-6-astra/openai-codex)
were quota-guarded "until 2026-11-20T22:40Z" with all 3 codex accounts walled for 6.5 days. The ask filed
from it (t_01a1d95da6382c64) said the default-model path lacks the far-wall same-class fallback pins get.

Why 1: the cards were held 05:44Z-09:20Z because the class's only other route was walled too. Evidence:
t_01a1d85b7b4a9e6d was rerouted default+quota_reroute to anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 at 05:44:40Z and exited 75
"Subscription quota unavailable for anthropic/claude-opus-5-5; resets at 1794648000" (09:20:00Z, the anthropic
5 h session window); alternate_route then excluded walled anthropic, so decision() correctly held.
Why 2: the fallback exists and worked: all 8 cards dispatched model_tier default+quota_reroute ->
anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 between 09:22:46Z and 09:26:04Z, unpinned, within one pickup cycle of that reset
(decision -> alternate_route / _strong_fallback; resolve_dispatch_tier -> _class_alternate_off_wall for fresh cards).
Why 3 (why it was filed as a missing fallback): every deadline the guard reports came from hold_until(), the
max reset of the episode's own walls: the worker pickup skip ("quota_hold ... until 2026-11-20T22:40Z (local
dispatch would hold it)"), the dispatcher stuck-warning suffix, chat-wait notices and the episode notice ("wait
until 11-20"). None said the hold actually ended at 09:20Z when anthropic reset.
Root (happened): the reported hold clock ignores the walls on the fallback routes that decision() waits on.
Root (not caught): tests pinned guard_hold_until only to the episode's own walls (test_kanban_quota_episode_walls
(c)); no test had a fallback route behind a shorter wall.
Recurrence: first report of this clock; codex weekly walls recur, so it would be filed again.

Fix: kanban_quota_episode.release_at(): the earliest known wall reset (provider file + episode walls) at which
decision() admits the card, else hold_until(). Used by guard_hold_until (stuck warning, chat wait), the worker
pickup quota_hold detail and the episode notice. Dispatch decisions are unchanged.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_quota_episode_release_at.py. RED on origin/main:
guard_hold_until == 1800561600 (codex reset) != 1800010800 (anthropic reset); GREEN after; the same test shows
the card runs on anthropic just past that reset. 36 quota/clock/pickup/chat-wait consumer files: 589 passed.
